TripGraph system hosting requirements (validated on this host)

Host baseline
- OS: Ubuntu 20.10 (Groovy)
- CPU arch: x86_64
- Java: OpenJDK 17 (required by Neo4j 5/2026.x)
- Python runtime: Python 3.9.x (project virtualenv at .venv)
- Node runtime: Node.js 20.x via nvm
- npm: 10.x

Installed system-level dependencies
1. Docker engine (already present on host)
2. Docker Compose v2 CLI (docker compose)
3. OpenJDK 17 JRE (openjdk-17-jre-headless)
4. Neo4j Community from official apt repository
5. Python 3.9 + venv tooling
6. nvm + Node.js 20 LTS

Why local hosting (non-container) was used
- Docker Hub pull is blocked on this network path, so docker compose cannot pull neo4j:5-community image.
- Local apt/pip/npm channels are reachable and were used successfully.

Required runtime configuration
- Create .env from .env.example
- Minimum required secret: GOOGLE_API_KEY
- For local Neo4j service, use:
  NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
- For frontend to hit backend on port 8000, use:
  VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

Corporate proxy note
- This host routes HTTP requests through a proxy chain.
- Always bypass proxy for loopback service calls:
  no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1

Local launch commands (recommended for this host)
1) Start Neo4j service
   sudo systemctl start neo4j

2) Start backend API
   cd /workspace/sw/siddaraj/iisc/deep_learning/TripGraph
   source .venv/bin/activate
   no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1 uvicorn backend.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

3) Start frontend
   export NVM_DIR="$HOME/.nvm" && . "$NVM_DIR/nvm.sh"
   cd /workspace/sw/siddaraj/iisc/deep_learning/TripGraph/frontend
   npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0

Connection endpoints
- Frontend UI: http://localhost:5173
- Backend API root/test console: http://localhost:8000/
- Backend Swagger docs: http://localhost:8000/docs
- Backend health: http://localhost:8000/health
- Neo4j Browser: http://localhost:7474
- Neo4j Bolt: bolt://localhost:7687

Operational checks
- Neo4j service status:
  sudo systemctl status neo4j --no-pager
- Backend health:
  no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1 curl -s http://localhost:8000/health
- Frontend dev server output:
  watch Vite terminal for Local/Network URLs

Optional container path (works only if Docker Hub access is available)
- docker compose up -d neo4j backend
- If using compose networking, set NEO4J_URI=bolt://neo4j:7687 in .env
